WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:18.727
Zoe was listening to Chase Gibson's newest song while doing research for her hero project.

2
00:00:18.728 --> 00:00:27.611
Her project partner, Amanda, had already made a list of possible heroes—all politicians, artists, and scientists.

3
00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:32.709
"Boring," Zoe thought after reading about Amanda's fifth-choice pick.

4
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.234
Amanda had already said no to Zoe's first choice—Chase Gibson.

5
00:00:37.235 --> 00:00:39.391
He was her favorite singer.

6
00:00:39.392 --> 00:00:42.480
And he could dance and act too.

7
00:00:42.481 --> 00:00:47.089
"But how has he changed the world?" Amanda had asked at school that day.

8
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.793
"Besides, I read he isn't even that nice."

9
00:00:50.794 --> 00:00:52.615
Zoe didn't care.

10
00:00:52.616 --> 00:00:57.634
Maybe she could still persuade Amanda that Chase was talented enough to write about.

11
00:00:57.635 --> 00:01:02.474
Taking a break, she pulled up the official Chase Gibson fan website.

12
00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:05.170
She could hardly believe her eyes.

13
00:01:05.171 --> 00:01:09.180
"Aaah!" Zoe's scream echoed through the house.

14
00:01:09.181 --> 00:01:11.264
"Zoe, what's wrong? What happened?"

15
00:01:11.265 --> 00:01:14.446
Zoe turned around to see Mom in the doorway.

16
00:01:14.447 --> 00:01:18.807
"Chase Gibson is coming to the mall this Saturday to sign autographs!"

17
00:01:18.808 --> 00:01:24.547
Mom frowned. "Never scream like that, unless you're hurt or in danger."

18
00:01:24.548 --> 00:01:27.076
"Can I go? Please, Mom!"

19
00:01:27.077 --> 00:01:31.230
"You and Amanda are working on your project on Saturday," Mom said.

20
00:01:31.231 --> 00:01:33.901
"Schoolwork comes first, you know."

21
00:01:33.902 --> 00:01:37.026
"But Mom!" Zoe pleaded.

22
00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:40.180
"Zoe, no," Mom said firmly.

23
00:01:40.181 --> 00:01:44.382
"Now turn that music down please. Dinner will be ready soon."

24
00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:49.805
Zoe slouched down and lowered the volume as Mom headed downstairs.

25
00:01:49.806 --> 00:01:54.915
"I have to go to the mall this Saturday," she thought.

26
00:01:54.916 --> 00:02:00.258
After waiting in line for over an hour, Zoe finally stepped up to the table.

27
00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:06.094
Seeing Chase Gibson in person made her forget all about the big lie she'd told her mother.

28
00:02:06.095 --> 00:02:10.247
"Hi, Chase! I'm your biggest fan!" Zoe said to the star.

29
00:02:10.248 --> 00:02:13.521
"Can you sign some things To Zoe, without a y?"

30
00:02:13.522 --> 00:02:18.216
She emptied her backpack filled with Chase Gibson merchandise onto the table.

31
00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:22.627
Chase Gibson looked at Zoe and then at the pile of stuff.

32
00:02:22.628 --> 00:02:26.106
"I can't sign all that!" he snapped.

33
00:02:26.107 --> 00:02:28.502
"I've been signing autographs for hours!

34
00:02:28.503 --> 00:02:32.957
And look at that line!"

35
00:02:32.958 --> 00:02:37.133
Zoe felt a lump in her throat. "But I'm your—"

36
00:02:37.134 --> 00:02:41.227
"Biggest fan? Yes, I know. That's what everyone says.

37
00:02:41.228 --> 00:02:44.080
Now pick one thing, and I'll sign it.

38
00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:46.345
Let's keep this line moving."

39
00:02:46.346 --> 00:02:49.439
Zoe shyly unrolled a small poster.

40
00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.619
Chase Gibson quickly scribbled an autograph on it.

41
00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.520
As Zoe walked away from the table, she looked at the autograph:

42
00:02:56.521 --> 00:03:03.636
To Zoey, —Chase Gibson it read in big ugly letters. "Ugh."

43
00:03:03.637 --> 00:03:06.270
Just then her phone beeped.

44
00:03:06.271 --> 00:03:08.704
It was a text message from Mom.

45
00:03:08.705 --> 00:03:11.955
Come home right now!

46
00:03:11.956 --> 00:03:17.258
"You lied about where you were going!" Mom's eyes narrowed.

47
00:03:17.259 --> 00:03:21.174
"I had no idea where you were when Amanda's mom called!

48
00:03:21.175 --> 00:03:24.592
Then I remembered that Chase Gibson was at the mall today."

49
00:03:24.593 --> 00:03:29.082
Zoe winced at hearing that name. "I'm sorry, Mom."

50
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.134
"I'll talk with you about some consequences later.

51
00:03:32.135 --> 00:03:33.797
For now, go to your room.

52
00:03:33.798 --> 00:03:36.564
Amanda will be here soon to work on your project.

53
00:03:36.565 --> 00:03:38.684
I hope you've learned a lesson!"

54
00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:42.540
"Oh, I learned a big lesson today," Zoe murmured.

55
00:03:42.541 --> 00:03:45.015
Zoe trudged off to her room.

56
00:03:45.016 --> 00:03:50.404
She flung her backpack, still filled with Chase Gibson stuff, onto the floor.

57
00:03:50.405 --> 00:03:52.594
She reached for her notebook.

58
00:03:52.595 --> 00:03:56.081
A Chase Gibson sticker smiled at her on the cover.

59
00:03:56.082 --> 00:03:58.377
Zoe stared back at him.

60
00:03:58.378 --> 00:04:00.549
"I still like your music.

61
00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:04.058
But Amanda was right—you're not a hero."

62
00:04:04.059 --> 00:04:11.205
She flipped open the notebook and began searching for a hero from Amanda's list.
